  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Passing triangle 3 v 1",
  "description": "Groups of four with one ball. Three players form a triangle 4–5 metres apart and the fourth stands in the middle as defender. The triangle passes it round and counts the passes out loud. Ten in a row wins, but if the defender wins the ball, they win. Change defender after every round. Lob passes over the defender are not allowed.\n\nWith uneven numbers an adult can fill a spot, or one group plays 4 v 1. Avoid 2 v 1 – there is no choice about who is open.\n\nVary it: a bigger triangle is easier for the passers, a smaller one harder. Progressions: the ball must move within two seconds, encourage bounce passes, or play 4 v 2. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Read who is open before you pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Use pass fakes and pivots to find a new angle – and avoid travelling."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Receiver: hands ready and eyes on the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Defender: low stance and arms out – make yourself big."
    }
  ],
